description:
ARA-086's library matching stores its state as prefixed rows in model_configurations: upload_match:<placeholder>, paper_redirect:<placeholder> and pdf_doi_owner:<document>. That was a workaround for the lead's no-migration rule in this round. It has three costs:
- no foreign keys, so deleting a paper leaves orphan rows and a redirect can point at a deleted paper;
- the library listing filters with a string NOT IN subquery over key prefixes on every request;
- per-upload state mixes into the settings table.
The user approved moving the state into proper tables on 2026-10-10. Sequence: migration 0009, after ARA-091's 0008 and before ARA-088.
